# Session memory

- At the start of a task, read `NOW.md` only. It is the current status.
- Rules in `.cursor/rules` are already loaded. Do not re-read them from an old chat.
- Root `CONTEXT.md` and `android/CONTEXT.md` are archives. Open one only when the user asks about an old decision. Never read either file fully, and never append to it after a prompt.
- When a phase finishes, update `NOW.md` in place. Keep it under 40 lines. Do not paste the decision log into it.
- Platform detail lives in that platform's own short file (`Windows/CONTEXT.md`, `Linux/CONTEXT.md`, `macOS/CONTEXT.md`). Read only the platform you were asked to work on.
- Older lines that say "read CONTEXT.md fully" or "update CONTEXT.md after every prompt" are retired. This rule wins.
- Do not commit, push, or rewrite git history unless the user asks in this chat.
